WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.069
New Jersey has a severe pension crisis.

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:10.830
The unfunded liabilities for pensions is

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.530
95 billion dollars. The entire New Jersey

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.320
state budget is 35 billion dollars. New

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.029
Jersey does not have the money to pay

00:00:18.029 --> 00:00:20.130
for these pensions. How did New Jersey get

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.300
into this situation?

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.460
The simple answer is that it is a direct

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.560
result of the enormous political power

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.390
of the New Jersey Education Association,

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:29.999
the state's largest teachers union. Over

00:00:29.999 --> 00:00:31.650
the course of the last 20 years,

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.800
NJEA has spent over 800 million dollars

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.230
on its various political tools. With that

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:37.980
kind of money,

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.199
NJEA got what it wanted on pensions.

00:00:40.199 --> 00:00:43.829
Recently NJEA sought to enshrine this

00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:45.120
bankrupt system in the state

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.430
constitution. Senate President Steve

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:50.670
Sweeney stood up to NJEA. NJEA then

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:54.059
exacted revenge by vowing to support

00:00:54.059 --> 00:00:55.800
senator Sweeney's opponent in the

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.170
Democratic gubernatorial primary and

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.120
forcing Sweeney to withdraw from the

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.910
race. Now NJEA has a politician who will

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:03.899
do its bidding,

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:07.350
thus encapsulating the New Jersey pension crisis.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.240
I'd like to know what you think about

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.250
New Jersey's pension crisis.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.110
Let us know in the comments section, and

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:15.150
also let us know what other topics you

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:18.000
want AEI scholars to cover in 60 seconds.

